{
  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "treatment of a calumniator. साश्चर्यचर्याः—आश्चर्यसहिता admirable,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "चर्या ( चरितम् ) येषां ते. The fig. here is विरोधाभास.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 70. भूरिविलम्बिनः—hanging very low. This reading is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "preferable to भूमि० as the point here is नम्रत्व. अनुद्धताः—Not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "haughty. समृद्धिभिः—with the acquisition of wealth. This sl.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "occurs in the S'âk. Act. V. The figures in this sl. according",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "to Râghavabhatta are क्रियादीपक. मालाप्रतिवस्तूपमा ( विनयस्य साधा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "रणधर्मस्य नम्रदूरविलम्ब्यनुद्धतशब्देनोक्तेः ), अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा and अर्थान्तरन्यास",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "( स्वभाव इत्यादिस्तु हिशब्दानुपादानेऽर्थान्तरन्यासः ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 71 Cf. sl. 65. supra. The fig. here is परिसंख्या as the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "S'âstras &c. are specially mentioned as imparting beauty to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the ear &c. to the exclusion of the ear-ornaments &c. It is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "thus defined–किंचित्पृष्टमपृष्टं वा कथितं यत्प्रकल्पते । तादृगन्यव्यपोहाय",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "परिसंख्या तु सा स्मृता ॥ K. P. X.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 72. पापात्—That from which a person is warded off is put",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "in the abl. case; see. com. हिताय योजयते—may mean ( 1 ) हितं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "साधयितुं ( हितकरे कर्मणि ) मित्रं प्रवर्तयति urges ( his friend ) to apply",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "himself to a work beneficial to him; or ( 2 ) आत्मानं योजयते—sets",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "himself about the accomplishment of his friend’s good. The dat.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "is to be explained by ‘ क्रियार्थोपपदस्य च कर्मणि स्थानिनः’ Pân. II.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "3. 14. When an infinitive of purpose is not actually used in a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "sentence its object is put in the dat. case; फलेभ्यो याति, फलान्याहर्तुं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "यातीत्यर्थः Sid. Kau.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 73 विकचीकरोति—causes to bloom, opens. A denom. verb",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "derived from विकच with the aff च्वि ( ई ). विकच-विगतः कचः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "( fold ) अस्मात्; full blown or expanded कैरव-a white lotus. Like",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "कुमुद it is a lotus blooming at moon-rise. चक्रवाल—a collection of;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "properly a circle of; चक्रवालं तु मण्डलम् । Amara. नाभ्यर्थितः to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "taken with all the three—दिनकर, चन्द्र and जलधर. अभियोग—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "application, resolutely setting oneself about. Fig Arthântaranyâsa.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 74. एते—Mr. Telang reads एके ‘some’. ते एते, however,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "serves as a better correlative of ये and gives proper force to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "main assertion. घटकाः—who bring about, accomplish. उद्यमभृतः—",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
